syntax:
template<class InputIterator, class Function>
Function for_each(InputIterator first, InputIterator last, Function f);
// Implementation notes: 'first' and 'last' must satisfy InputIterator requirements. 'f' is applied to *iter for each iter in [first, last). The compiler may inline 'f' if it's a lambda or simple functor. For mutable iterators, 'f' can modify elements, affecting memory layout directly.
